        "5": {
          "id": "5",
          "name": "index.html",
          "contents": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n  <head>\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"style.css\">\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    \n    <!-- Title -->\n    <h1>Mysteries Unveiled: The Secrets of Ancient Civilizations</h1>\n    \n    <!-- informational paragraph -->\n    <p>Dive into the depths of history to uncover the mysteries that ancient civilizations left behind. From the architectural marvels of the Egyptians to the advanced astronomical knowledge of the Mayans, each civilization carried its own secrets and innovations. These societies have shaped our understanding of engineering, astronomy, mathematics, and philosophy. Explore the remnants of these ancient worlds to discover the genius that laid the foundations for modern science and culture.</p> \n    \n    <!-- gallery for image and link -->\n    <div class=\"gallery\">\n      <div class=\"link-card\">\n        <div>\n          <img src=\"pyramids.png\" alt=\"Egyptian pyramids\">\n        </div>\n        <div>\n          <a class=\"egyptians\" href=\"egyptians.html\">Find out how the Egyptians build the pyramids!</a>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    \n      <div class=\"link-card\">\n        <div>\n          <img src=\"mayanGlyphs.png\" alt=\"Mayan glyphs\">\n        </div>\n        <div>\n          <a class=\"mayans\" href=\"mayans.html\">Find out more about the Mayan's advanced knowledge of astronomy and technology!</a>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"citation\">\n      <p>All images created by chatGPT<br>CC0 1.0</p>\n    </div>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  </body>\n</html>",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": false
        },
        "6": {
          "id": "6",
          "name": "mayans.html",
          "contents": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n  <head>\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"style.css\">\n  </head>\n  <body>\n\n    <a class=\"back-link\" href=\"index.html\">Back to Mysteries Unveiled</a>\n\n    <h1>The Mayans' Advanced Knowledge of Astronomy</h1>\n\n    <div class=\"page-image\">\n      <img src=\"observatory-mayans.jpg\" alt=\"El Caracol, the round Mayan astronomical observatory at Chichen Itza\">\n    </div>\n\n    <p>The ancient Maya were extraordinary astronomers who tracked the sky with an accuracy that still impresses scientists today. Without telescopes or modern instruments, they observed the movements of the sun, moon, and planets over centuries, recording what they saw in bark-paper books called codices and carving it into stone monuments.</p>\n\n    <p>One of their most remarkable achievements was the calendar system. The Maya used several calendars at once, including a 365-day solar calendar and a 260-day ritual calendar, which combined to form a 52-year cycle. They also calculated the length of the solar year to within a few minutes of its true value, a feat that took European astronomers many more centuries to match.</p>\n\n    <p>The Maya tracked Venus with incredible precision, using it to time important events like wars and coronations. Structures such as the observatory at Chichen Itza, known as El Caracol, have windows aligned to the rising and setting points of Venus and other celestial bodies on key dates throughout the year.</p>\n\n    <p>This astronomical knowledge wasn't just academic. It shaped agriculture, religion, and politics, helping the Maya know when to plant crops, when to hold ceremonies, and when omens favored major decisions.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"citation\">\n      <p>Photo by <a href=\"https://unsplash.com/@lukearam?utm_source=unsplash&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=creditCopyText\">LARAM</a> on <a href=\"https://unsplash.com/photos/ancient-stone-observatory-building-with-stairs-and-grass-c7_urbZ8w-A?utm_source=unsplash&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=creditCopyText\">Unsplash</a></p>\n    </div>\n\n  </body>\n</html>\n",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": false
        },
        "7": {
          "id": "7",
          "name": "egyptians.html",
          "contents": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n  <head>\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"style.css\">\n  </head>\n  <body>\n\n    <a class=\"back-link\" href=\"index.html\">Back to Mysteries Unveiled</a>\n\n    <h1>How Did the Egyptians Build the Pyramids?</h1>\n\n    <div class=\"page-image\">\n      <img src=\"pyramids-egyptians.jpg\" alt=\"The pyramids of Giza in the Egyptian desert\">\n    </div>\n\n    <p>The pyramids of Giza were built more than 4,500 years ago, and their construction is still one of the great engineering mysteries of the ancient world. Historians and archaeologists have pieced together the story using tomb inscriptions, worker records, and the remains of the ramps and tools left behind.</p>\n\n    <p>Most researchers now agree that the Egyptians moved massive limestone blocks, some weighing several tons, using long ramps built from mudbrick, limestone chips, and packed sand. As the pyramid grew taller, workers likely extended or wrapped these ramps around the structure so that blocks could be dragged upward on wooden sledges. Wetting the sand in front of the sledges reduced friction, letting large teams of workers pull the loads with less effort.</p>\n\n    <p>Recent excavations near the pyramid sites have uncovered ramps with post holes cut into the stone, suggesting rope-and-post systems that helped haul blocks up steeper sections. Papyrus logs from a harbor worker named Merer even describe boat crews ferrying limestone down the Nile to the construction site.</p>\n\n    <p>Far from being built by slaves, evidence from nearby worker villages shows the pyramids were constructed by a rotating labor force of skilled workers and farmers, who were fed, housed, and even given medical care during their service.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"citation\">\n      <p>Photo by <a href=\"https://unsplash.com/@osamaabosaadia?utm_source=unsplash&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=creditCopyText\">Osama Elsayed</a> on <a href=\"https://unsplash.com/photos/brown-pyramid-under-blue-sky-during-daytime-vqRMXgVtGXM?utm_source=unsplash&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=creditCopyText\">Unsplash</a></p>\n    </div>\n\n  </body>\n</html>\n",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": false
        },
        "8": {
          "id": "8",
          "name": "style.css",
          "contents": "/* FIND AND FIX THE BUGS FOR THE ANCHOR TAG STATES */\n\n.egyptians.link {\n  font-family:Arial;\n  color:#0014ff;\n  font-size: 18px;\n}\n\negyptians.hover {\n  color: #f7f8fd;\n  background-color: #2f35ff;\n  font-size: 24px;\n  text-decoration-style: wavy;\n  border-radius: 7px;\n}\n\n.mayans.link {\n  font-family:Verdana;\n  color:#a80707;\n  font-size: 18px;\n}\n\nmayans:hover {\n  color: #f7f8fd;\n  background-color: #a80707;\n  font-size: 24px;\n  text-decoration-style: wavy;\n  border-radius: 7px;\n}\n\n/* body style */\nbody {\n  background-color: #ffd9d9;\n  text-align: center;\n}\n\nh1 {\n  font-family: Arial;\n  font-size: 36px;\n  text-align: center;\n}\n\np {\n  font-family: Arial;\n  font-size: 18px;\n}\n\n.gallery {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: row;\n  justify-content: space-around;\n  align-items: center;\n}\n\n.link-card {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  align-items: center;\n  justify-content: center;\n}\n\n\nimg {\n  border-style: solid;\n  border-radius: 15px;\n  width: 300px;\n  margin: 15px;\n}\n\n.citation {\n  height: 300px;\n  display: flex;\n  align-items: flex-end;\n}\n\n.citation > p {\n  text-align: center;\n  font-style: italic;\n  font-size: 10px;\n}\n\n/* styles for the new egyptians.html and mayans.html pages */\n.back-link {\n  margin: 15px;\n  font-family: Arial;\n  font-size: 16px;\n  color: #2f35ff;\n  text-decoration: none;\n}\n\n.back-link:hover {\n  text-decoration: underline;\n}\n\n.page-image {\n  display: flex;\n  justify-content: center;\n}\n\n.page-image img {\n  width: 400px;\n}",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": true
        },
